WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.634
-Welcome, welcome,
welcome to the show.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.601
And I love that -- that pop.
-Oh, the pop.

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:05.834
Oh, baby, I can teach you
the pop.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:07.701
Here. Look at this.
That's for you, Jimmy.

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:08.968
-Really?
-Yes. You know, I'm Shangela.

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.133
I come with gifts, baby.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:12.067
Alright. Now, look.
If you want to do this --

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.667
I taught this to
the Vice President, as well,

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:14.734
Kamala Harris,
the Vice President.

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:15.934
-Yes.
-Yes, indeed.

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:18.434
So, it goes like this --
whaaa! -- just like that.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.267
Hold with the thumb,
release with the fore.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:21.467
You ready?
-Okay.

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:22.934
Hold with the thumb,
release with the fore.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:25.067
-I believe in you.
[ Drum roll ]

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:26.968
-I've never popped...
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:29.567
-...I mean, a fan.
-Oh!

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:30.868
[ Laughter ]
-I've never done this.

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:32.300
-Yes, yes.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.968
Ha!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.400
-That was alright.
-That was lovely.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.634
That was lovely.
-No.

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.133
But you know what?
-No.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.868
-You know, that was lovely,
but I'm Shangela.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.801
-[ Laughs ]
-I'm a coach. I'm a mentor.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.100
I'm a professional.
-That's right.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.634
-And I strive
for the best with you.

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:48.167
-That was not the best.
-But you can get there.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.667
-Okay.
-So, here we go.

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:53.100
I want you to give it fever,
fire, and ferocious fierceness.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.300
Are you ready?
-Yes.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.100
-Grab -- there you go.
And release the fore.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.300
I want you to give it
some gusto, Jimmy.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.467
Oh, oh, Jimmy.

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.167
Okay, here we go.
-[ Chuckling ] Oh, okay.

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.667
-Look, baby. Hold.
-Oh, yeah, hold, yeah.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:04.767
-And release with the fore.
-And release.

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:06.567
-You got it. Ready?
-Yeah.

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:09.901
-One, two, three.
[ Drum roll ]

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.767
-Ha!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.601
Come on. Yes!

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:14.934
-Let me try.
Let me try.

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:16.234
Ready? Drum roll. Here we go.
-Here we go. And...

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:19.634
[ Drum roll ]
One, two, three.

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:21.968
Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:24.434
Yes, indeed, better.
-That's what I'm saying.

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.634
-That was better.
-I love you, by the way.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:27.868
I'm just happy.

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:29.200
I just want to clarify something

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.667
before we continue the
interview -- cover one thing.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.567
-Yes, I'm a man and all this.
I know.

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.634
That's what you were gonna say.
-No, no, no, no, I know that.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.200
Not that question.
Not that question.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.434
I want to know -- you -- you --
you're -- you are not a deejay.

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.968
-No. Ooh, thank you,
I must clarify that, as well.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:45.767
Because -- I say D.J.
because my mom --

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:48.567
Hi, Mom. Hi, Grangela.
Hi, fam.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.033
[ Laughter ]
My mom named me D.J.,

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:52.801
Darius Jeremy.
-Yes.

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:54.767
-Okay? People think that
I'm an actual deejay,

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.300
but I don't have that talent.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.601
However, you know -- you know,
if they pay me enough,

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:01.234
I'll get behind a keyboard,
a laptop, and push some buttons.

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:02.834
I'll be
the Paris Hilton of drag!

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.400
Yes!
-[ Laughs ] Alright.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.300
You can get back there
and press some buttons, yeah.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.133
But you are not a deejay,
so, no,

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.334
don't think that you're
gonna do -- deejay some gig.

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.067
-No, out of drag,
my name is D.J.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.634
In drag, Shangela.
-Yeah.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.033
-Not a deejay.
[ Audience cheers ]

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:17.300
-Now, a lot of people know you
from "RuPaul's Drag Race."

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.634
And -- But you didn't really
last that long the first --

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.300
when --
you were on one episode.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.534
-That is true.
-But you did a genius move.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.434
Can you explain to everyone
what -- what you did?

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:28.334
-Well, you know, I am
a working girl, a professional.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:29.734
-Mm.
-And I've been a part

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:31.467
of the "RuPaul's Drag Race"
family for years.

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.968
I've been there
a number of times.

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:35.934
My first time there, Season 2,
I thought I was about to win,

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:37.234
'cause you know I go
in any room thinking,

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:38.267
"Oh, baby,
I'm about to turn the party."

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:39.601
-Oh, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:41.934
-Well, I was
the first one voted out.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:43.667
I'd only been doing drag
for five months,

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:45.767
and I remember getting
to the house and thinking,

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:48.467
"I quit my job for this.
What am I going to do?"

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:51.167
But I had to get up out of
that moment and go to work.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:52.734
And what I did
is I started calling

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:53.968
different clubs
and booking myself.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.834
'Cause we had a time,
like three months,

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:58.300
between the time they announced
you were on the show

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.567
to when you actually, like,

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:01.133
appeared on the show.
-Okay.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:02.868
-So, I started calling clubs
saying, uh [clears throat]

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:05.200
"Uh, hello."
That's my man voice, okay?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.801
-Mm.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:07.868
Sounds like
my Shangela voice, too.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:10.367
[ Laughter ]
I was like,

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:11.567
"You really need
to book Shangela.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.000
She is fabulous."

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.334
And so I would get them under
contract to have my booking.

00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:16.400
So when the show came out,
they said,

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.400
"Baby,
you're the first one out."

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.601
I said, "Baby, don't worry.

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.267
I'm a repeat customer
kind of girl."

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:21.701
And I went in
and turned the party.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.200
-Yeah.
So, you booked yourself...

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
I think it's brilliant.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.300
You book yourself before even
people saw you on the show.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.601
And you go, "Trust me. You're
gonna want to know Shangela."

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.033
-Oh, yeah.
I was booking myself.

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:35.200
You know,
I went to SMU in Dallas.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.734
I was also writing
my own press releases

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.000
at the time.
-Wow.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.400
-I was a one-stop-shop
kind of diva.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.367
-Now look at you.
Look at what you've done.

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:46.267
I mean, you've done things with
Lady Gaga, with Ariana Grande.

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:50.834
I heard that you once performed
as Beyoncé for Beyoncé.

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:53.133
-True story.
And I'm going to tell you --

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, yes, baby, the dolls.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:57.167
The divas.
I love Lady Gaga.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:58.567
I love Ariana.

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:02.667
And Beyoncé, is, like, my doll,
my Duchess, my idol.

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:03.801
I love her so much.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:06.200
She was the first number
I ever performed in 2009

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.734
when I first started drag.

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:11.100
So, when she was being honored
at the GLAAD Awards in 2019,

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.567
they asked me -- they said,

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:14.501
"Shangela, would you like to
perform a number for Beyoncé?"

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:16.267
I said,
"No, I would like to perform

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:17.601
nine numbers for her, please."
-Exactly.

00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:18.868
-A medley.
-Exactly!

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:20.167
-Yes! And I did.

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:21.667
And I remember seeing
at the end,

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:24.000
she and Jay-Z both gave me
a standing ovation.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.868
And I was like, "Oh, my God.
I love them so much."

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:29.300
-And did you get to --
did you get to meet them at all

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.367
or talk...?
-Meet Beyoncé?

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:31.534
-Yeah.
-Oh, baby.

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:32.734
I wasn't leaving that building
till I did.

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:34.000
-That's right.
-No. [ Laughs ]

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.400
[ Laughter ]
-No, she was so kind.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.200
She was like, "Yes,
I would love to meet Shangela."

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.467
So they took me to, like,

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.901
this room
where she was meeting people.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:41.934
And I was standing there --
you know,

00:04:41.934 --> 00:04:43.167
dressed as Beyoncé
standing there.

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:44.300
And I look up,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.767
and I'm standing next to Jay-Z.
-Yeah.

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:48.400
-And I was like, "Oh, my God,
I'm next to Jay-Z!

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.934
I need to say something cool."

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:51.634
'Cause, you know, I want to be
invited to the house to kick it.

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:52.667
You know?
-Yeah.

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:53.968
-I wanted him to know I'm cool.

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:58.501
So, I was like, "So,
you're from New York, right?"

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:01.701
And he goes,
"Yo, Brooklyn, come on, now."

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:04.033
I was like, "Yes, Brooklyn!
That's right!

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:06.167
I'm from Paris, Texas."

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:07.667
Yeah, he didn't laugh
at my joke.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:10.734
He was really sweet.

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:12.334
And then I went over
to meet Beyoncé.

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:14.367
And she was like -- you know,
she's the Queen Bey, okay?

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:15.701
-Yeah.
-She just glow --

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.234
I was like, "Where is
that light coming from?"

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:18.534
But it was just her.
She was glowing.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:21.167
-Yeah, she's glowing.
-And, honestly, she was so kind.

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:23.334
She was like,
"You were so good."

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:24.834
-Really?
-I was like, "You're so good."

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.400
Like, she was amazing.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.834
-Just repeating her words
back to her.

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:30.300
-I literally was erupting
everything she said

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.767
back to her.
-Yeah.

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:33.667
-I couldn't think of anything
to say, but I love her.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:36.467
-Well, you -- you are glowing,
and you glow.

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:40.067
When you see "We're Here" --
I loved it so much.

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:42.667
Not only is it --
are you funny in it,

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:45.834
but it is so cool,
it is so positive,

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:47.801
and it's emotional.

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:50.100
Like, I really -- I needed a fan
when I watch it.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.334
When I watch you...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:53.033
-You either need a fan,
or you need a Kleenex.

00:05:53.033 --> 00:05:54.434
You know,
'cause I always keep a Kleenex

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:55.968
somewhere near my [bleep].
-Yep.

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:57.267
-Just in case, honey.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.267 --> 00:05:59.868
-No the show "We're Here" --
I love to tell people --

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:01.100
you didn't see that one coming,
did you?

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.234
-No, that was a good one.
-You can have that.

00:06:02.234 --> 00:06:03.901
-Thank you. Oh, my gosh.
I appreciate it.

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:05.701
-That's a [bleep] tissue
for Jimmy, yes.

00:06:05.701 --> 00:06:06.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:07.934
-That's what it's called?
I love it.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:09.234
-Yes.
-I'm putting this --

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:10.701
I'm putting this in a frame.
-Wonderful.

00:06:10.701 --> 00:06:12.334
But, you know, our show --

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:13.968
I'm so happy to host this show
with my friends,

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:15.033
Bob the Drag Queen...
-He's great.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.167
-...and Eureka.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:18.167
The show is educational...
-Yeah.

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:20.801
-...for those who aren't
familiar with the struggles,

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:22.934
and, also, the triumphs
of the queer community.

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:25.868
But, also, the show is
emotional, as you said,

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:27.234
and entertaining.
-Yeah.

00:06:27.234 --> 00:06:29.400
-So, baby, it's some of
the best drag on TV.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.901
And you don't have to be a
member of the LGBTQI+ community

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:36.501
to know that this is something
that people deserve to see.

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:38.634
Because we all need to be --
you know,

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:40.033
we need to feel something.
-Yeah.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:41.834
-And this show makes you feel
something, for sure.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:43.534
-Yeah, I love it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:43.534 --> 00:06:44.901
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:47.701
Here's Shangela in this Monday's
episode of "We're Here."

00:06:47.701 --> 00:06:48.901
Take a look at this.

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:50.534
-Before you speak out
for anybody else,

00:06:50.534 --> 00:06:52.100
we got to work here.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.067
There is a way to be happy.

00:06:54.067 --> 00:06:56.067
Even if it doesn't come
in the dream

00:06:56.067 --> 00:06:58.100
to get a call from everybody
in our family saying,

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.934
"We love you.
We were wrong.

00:06:59.934 --> 00:07:01.901
We apologize.
We're sorry."

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:04.501
That'd be beautiful.
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:04.501 --> 00:07:05.934
-But it might not happen.

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:08.033
So, you're going to
have to change

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:11.834
what you think happiness is,
okay?

00:07:11.834 --> 00:07:13.167
-Yeah.

00:07:13.167 --> 00:07:17.033
-Kais really needs to celebrate
who he has become.

00:07:17.033 --> 00:07:19.000
"I'm living
as an out, loud, and proud

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.567
Muslim Tunisian gay man."

00:07:21.567 --> 00:07:24.767
I want him to be able to say,
"It's okay to be me."

00:07:24.767 --> 00:07:26.067
♪♪

00:07:26.067 --> 00:07:27.200
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.200
-D.J. Shangela Pierce,
everybody.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.634
"We're Here" airs Mondays
at 9:00 p.m. on HBO.

00:07:35.634 --> 00:07:36.834
Can you give me a "halleloo"?

00:07:36.834 --> 00:07:38.234
-Oh, baby, you can always
get a "halleloo."

00:07:38.234 --> 00:07:39.300
-Yeah, that's right.
-Halleloo.

